  message: "Done. Shapes 1-4 in PR #1953 (d4bac1048a) and #1954 (c5ef72894e); shape 5 in PR #1960 (e7a90a03fd), after its precision audit found and fixed three js-module-linker wrong routes (WI-pulid #1956, WI-tufob #1957, WI-dunab #1959). Root causes: the cross-package guard refused a module-object / namespace member and a default import that WI-rilof's named-binding route would have accepted; an attribute read on an in-tree module object was emitted as a module_attr_ref stand-in; the analyzer's <spec>:0-0:module import stub survived beside the linker's file edge with nothing stating the relation. CLOSURE EVIDENCE, the filed fixture (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nuzas_10292026/fixtures/js) through production `hypergumbo survey` on merged dev: (1) b.helper() via const b = require('@ws/b') -> packages/b/src/index.js helper; (2) C.shout() via import * as C -> packages/c/src/index.ts shout; (3) cDefault() via a default import -> c's export default cDefault; (4) new b.Engine() -> references to class Engine, no @ws/b.Engine stand-in; (5) each of the 4 @ws/ module stand-ins (index.js:1, index.js:3 @ws/b/src/util/deep, test/a.test.js:1, esm.ts:1) carries superseded_by naming the file edge that resolved it (packages/b/src/index.js, packages/b/src/util/deep.js, packages/c/src/index.ts) -- INV-nuzas carve-out (c). check.py with carve-out (c): 0 violations. Control ctl_js: calls / instantiates / imports edge set identical to 10-27. Grant table docs/audits/0025: 6,792 resolutions over 7 repos, 6,213 judged, 0 wrong. Not asserted: consumers that count external nodes read superseded_by (ADR-0057's general gap)."  # fd4d
